    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d663">

                <pb facs="0703" n="585" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg585"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">312.1722 Sandino/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morrow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-30T14:00:00-06:00">April 30, 1929—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>230. Department’s 333, April 25, 9 p.m.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d663-f1"/> The
                    President informed me yesterday afternoon that Sandino would take up his
                    residence at <pb facs="0704" n="586" xml:id="pg586"/> Merida, Yucatan. He
                    assured me that Sandino would not be allowed to come to Mexico City en route to
                    Yucatan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morrow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d663-f1" n="27" xml:id="d663-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it repeated the text of telegram No. 52, April 24, 9 a.m., from the
                    Chargé in Guatemala, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
